<title>Terms and Conditions</title>
<intro>
This document represents a binding agreement between the user and the "Teras" application, and governs the use of the services provided through the application.
</intro>

<sections>
<id>1</id>
<title>Available Services</title>
<items>
<text>The Teras application provides the following services:</text>
<type>plain</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>On-site electronic vehicle inspection at the customer location.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Comprehensive vehicle maintenance services.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Bodywork, denting, and painting services.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
</sections>

<sections>
<id>2</id>
<title>Fees and Refund Policy</title>

<subsections>
<id>2.1</id>
<title>Fees</title>
<items>
<text>On-site electronic inspection fee: 150 SAR.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Inspection and towing fee for maintenance or bodywork services: 250 SAR.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Additional fee for hydraulic tow truck usage when required: 100 SAR.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
</subsections>

<subsections>
<id>2.2</id>
<title>Refund Policy</title>
<items>
<text>The customer is entitled to request a refund only before service execution begins.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Service execution is considered to have started when:</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>The technician heads to the customer location.</text>
<type>bullet</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>The tow truck starts moving toward the customer location.</text>
<type>bullet</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>After execution begins, cancellation or refund is not allowed.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
</subsections>
</sections>

<sections>
<id>3</id>
<title>Reports and Approvals</title>

<items>
<text>After inspection or vehicle receipt, the application sends a technical report including:</text>
<type>plain</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Detected issues.</text>
<type>bullet</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Repair cost.</text>
<type>bullet</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Spare parts cost.</text>
<type>bullet</type>
</items>

<items>
<text>The customer has two options:</text>
<type>plain</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Approve and proceed with payment.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>Reject the report and cancel.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>

<extra>
<title>Edit Option</title>
<items>
<text>Before selecting (Approve and Pay), the customer can modify certain report items, such as removing specific repair items. After modification, they can proceed with approval and payment.</text>
<type>plain</type>
</items>
</extra>
</sections>

<sections>
<id>4</id>
<title>Warranty and Disclaimer</title>
<items>
<text>One-month warranty on repaired parts only, starting from the vehicle delivery date.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>The warranty does not cover unrepaired issues or items not approved in the report.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>The warranty does not cover misuse, accidents, or maintenance performed by third parties after repair.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
<items>
<text>All personal belongings must be removed from the vehicle before delivery. The application is not responsible for any lost items inside the vehicle.</text>
<type>number</type>
</items>
</sections>

<sections>
<id>5</id>
<title>Service Suspension or Refusal</title>
<items>
<text>Teras reserves the right to refuse or suspend service before execution begins if execution is not possible for any reason.</text>
<type>plain</type>
</items>
</sections>

<sections>
<id>6</id>
<title>Consent</title>
<items>
<text>Using the application implies that the user agrees to all terms and conditions contained in this document.</text>
<type>plain</type>
</items>
</sections>

